   = help: the trait `verum::sealed::private::SealedHas<Undeclared, There<There<Here>>>` is not implemented for `(Decl, (Elem, (Other, Junk)))`
   = note: Verum's sealed traits are implemented by Verum itself and by its derive macros. Writing the impl by hand grants something no declaration authorises, and nothing would report the difference.
note: required by a bound in `Has`
  --> src/typelevel.rs
   |
   | pub trait Has<T, Idx>: private::SealedHas<T, Idx> {}
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Has`
   = note: `Has` is a "sealed trait", because to implement it you also need to implement `verum::sealed::private::SealedHas`, which is not accessible; this is usually done to force you to use one of the provided types that already implement it
